From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt7988a-bpi-r4-pro: reserve
 Factory partition

The current upstream device tree assigns all SPI-NAND space after BL2 to
UBI. Reserve the 4 MiB Factory region used by the BPI/MediaTek vendor
layout and the previously tested local M03 implementation, then start UBI
at 6 MiB.

Do not describe NVMEM MAC cells here: no cell contents or consumers have
been verified for this board. M04 reads the raw Factory offsets only when
needed, while installation-layout consistency remains owned by M10.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 .../dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi
@@ -487,8 +487,13 @@
 		};
 
 		partition@200000 {
+			reg = <0x200000 0x400000>;
+			label = "Factory";
+		};
+
+		partition@600000 {
 			compatible = "linux,ubi";
-			reg = <0x200000 0xfe00000>;
+			reg = <0x600000 0xfa00000>;
 			label = "ubi";
 		};
 	};
-- 
2.51.0

